-- title:
--   Regularity of g dj at smooth special-fibre chart points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume the $q$-series [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of full level, i.e. in the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the relevant ratios of integral forms; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum of type [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81), and write $F$ for the $q$-expansion function field of the group $\Gamma_M(M,H)$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F$ whose elements are exactly those $f_0$ for which there are power series $a, a'$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} = \{q \in \mathbb{Q} : p \nmid \mathrm{den}(q)\}$ with $a' \not\equiv 0$ modulo $p$ (its image under [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAtResidue p`](def/GaloisRep_RatLocalizedAtResidue.html#L15) is nonzero) and $f_0 \cdot a' = a$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $\eta \in \Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfy $\eta = g\,dj$ for some $g \in W_0$, where $j \in F$ is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\mathbb{Q}$; assume further that for every valuation subring $O$ of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{Q}$ there are $c, t \in O$ with $\eta = c\,dt$. Let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime of the finite chart algebra, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$, such that: the image of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$; the image of $\mathfrak{p}$ under the underlying map of the finite-chart morphism [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.ιFin`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L47) lies in $\mathfrak{X}$'s smooth locus; every chart element $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$ has $s^{-1} \in W_0$; and the ideal generated by $p$ in the localisation of the chart algebra at $\mathfrak{p}$ is prime. Then there exist $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$ in the chart algebra, natural numbers $n, k$ and families $a, b : \mathrm{Fin}\,k \to$ chart algebra with $s^{n} \cdot \eta = \sum_{i} a_i\, d b_i$ in $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the smooth-point regularity step in extending the differential attached to a cusp form over a Deligne–Rapoport style integral model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$: Gauss-integrality of $g$ (no pole along the component at infinity) plus regularity on the generic fibre forces $\eta$ to be, after inverting one function nonvanishing at the point, a chart-algebra combination of chart differentials, which is the local form of regularity at the chosen special-fibre point. It is used in the $q$-expansion-principle argument [`CuspForm.exists_forall_isRegularAt_of_not_mem_ssPlacesQExp_diffQExp_eq_intSeriesC_of_isIntegralQExp_residueField`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_forall_isRegularAt_of_not_mem_ssPlacesQExp_diffQExp_eq_intSeriesC_of_isIntegralQExp_residueField).
-- source:
